00:01:30.265 --> 00:01:31.647
Hello and welcome to another edition

00:01:31.647 --> 00:01:33.006
of Modeling the Masters.

00:01:33.006 --> 00:01:34.621
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:01:34.621 --> 00:01:35.673
Today, we're going to be talking

00:01:35.673 --> 00:01:38.292
about the famous entrepreneur Walt Disney

00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:39.913
and how you can model his strategies

00:01:39.913 --> 00:01:43.080
to achieve success with your business.

00:02:09.965 --> 00:02:12.236
Everyone knows Walt Disney for his movies,

00:02:12.236 --> 00:02:14.559
theme parks, and cast of characters.

00:02:14.559 --> 00:02:17.050
What most people don't know
is when he first started out

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.776
he had no money, he had
to live in his office

00:02:19.776 --> 00:02:22.050
because he couldn't afford
rent for an apartment.

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.053
He survived on a diet of cold beans

00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:26.315
because he couldn't afford food.

00:02:26.315 --> 00:02:28.540
By committing to his
business and sticking with it

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.098
he was now able to build a business

00:02:30.098 --> 00:02:33.060
that has almost 40 billion
dollars in revenue.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.729
Today, we're going to
look at three lessons

00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:36.587
that you can learn from
Walt Disney's success

00:02:36.587 --> 00:02:38.670
and apply it into your company.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.365
Lesson number one is find
something that you love.

00:02:41.365 --> 00:02:43.663
Walt Disney grew up in the early 1900s

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:47.153
on a farm in Missouri and
developed a passion for drawing.

00:02:47.153 --> 00:02:49.501
So much so that one of his
neighbors actually paid him

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.125
to draw some cartoons of his horses.

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:53.769
When Walt Disney got to school he found

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:55.857
that he was a good student
but he really enjoyed

00:02:55.857 --> 00:02:59.154
doodling as opposed to paying
attention to his teachers.

00:02:59.154 --> 00:03:01.244
He connected with one of
his high school papers

00:03:01.244 --> 00:03:04.870
and started drawing patriotic
cartoons for the school paper.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.579
When he was 16, though,
he found that school

00:03:06.579 --> 00:03:08.012
just wasn't for him.

00:03:08.012 --> 00:03:10.383
So, he dropped out, joined the red cross,

00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:12.200
learned to become an ambulance driver,

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.464
and actually was shipped to France

00:03:13.464 --> 00:03:16.473
to become an ambulance driver over there.

00:03:16.473 --> 00:03:18.957
He couldn't lose that passion
for drawing and cartooning

00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:20.738
and he ended up plastering his ambulance

00:03:20.738 --> 00:03:23.461
full of different cartoon
creations that he had made.

00:03:23.461 --> 00:03:24.451
People knew him on the street

00:03:24.451 --> 00:03:25.772
because he was the ambulance driver

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:29.107
with all the different cartoons
plastered on his ambulance.

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:31.058
He decided that cartooning was for him,

00:03:31.058 --> 00:03:33.295
he was going to be an artist,
an he returned to America

00:03:33.295 --> 00:03:36.048
to start his career as an artist.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.507
So, lesson number one
really is make sure you have

00:03:38.507 --> 00:03:40.988
that strong passion for your business.

00:03:40.988 --> 00:03:42.192
If you don't really love it

00:03:42.192 --> 00:03:44.660
it's going to be hard to
succeed as a business owner.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.222
If you look at any famous entrepreneur

00:03:46.222 --> 00:03:47.563
and why they started their business,

00:03:47.563 --> 00:03:49.227
it wasn't for the money.

00:03:49.227 --> 00:03:51.020
Money comes when you're really passionate

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.495
about what you're doing.

00:03:52.495 --> 00:03:55.180
So, think about what is it
that you do in your spare time?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.555
What do you really enjoy doing?

00:03:56.555 --> 00:03:58.045
What gets you going in the morning?

00:03:58.045 --> 00:04:00.466
What are your hobbies and
how can you turn those

00:04:00.466 --> 00:04:03.075
into a potential business opportunity?

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.989
Lesson number two is push the boundaries.

00:04:05.989 --> 00:04:08.849
Walt Disney first made his mark in 1934,

00:04:08.849 --> 00:04:12.359
when he proposed making a
feature length animation

00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:14.003
which had never been done before.

00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:16.077
It was called Snow White.

00:04:16.077 --> 00:04:17.705
It took him three years to make,

00:04:17.705 --> 00:04:19.590
he went a hundred percent over budget,

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.754
people thought he was crazy for doing it,

00:04:21.754 --> 00:04:23.088
he ran out of money at the end

00:04:23.088 --> 00:04:26.007
and had to actually act out
the last scenes of the movie

00:04:26.007 --> 00:04:27.880
for his bankers to get the money he needed

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.864
to close and finish the movie.

00:04:29.864 --> 00:04:32.254
It ended up being a huge success.

00:04:32.254 --> 00:04:33.804
It was the biggest hit of the year.

00:04:33.804 --> 00:04:35.522
He won an Academy Award for it

00:04:35.522 --> 00:04:38.407
and it was a financial gain for him.

00:04:38.407 --> 00:04:41.573
Walt Disney's next big
project was Disneyland,

00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:45.100
a 330 acre project out in California.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.318
A theme park which had
nothing to do with his movies.

00:04:48.318 --> 00:04:49.762
People thought he was crazy again.

00:04:49.762 --> 00:04:50.907
"Why would you do this?

00:04:50.907 --> 00:04:53.163
"What tie does it have
to your movie business?"

00:04:53.163 --> 00:04:54.389
But he had a vision.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:55.921
He was determined to make it happen.

00:04:55.921 --> 00:04:58.237
And, again, it was a big success for him.

00:04:58.237 --> 00:05:01.156
Then he went on to open
up the Walt Disney World

00:05:01.156 --> 00:05:03.713
in Florida and the company
was able to open up

00:05:03.713 --> 00:05:06.111
different theme parks around the world.

00:05:06.111 --> 00:05:09.354
The message for entrepreneurs
here is push the boundaries.

00:05:09.354 --> 00:05:10.636
You need to do something different

00:05:10.636 --> 00:05:12.242
to get your company noticed.

00:05:12.242 --> 00:05:14.789
As a small entrepreneur,
there's so much competition.

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:16.918
It's so difficult to get
on people's radar screens

00:05:16.918 --> 00:05:18.381
and make them pay attention to you

00:05:18.381 --> 00:05:21.461
so you have to do something
that's going to get you noticed.

00:05:21.461 --> 00:05:23.852
Something that will help
you standout from the crowd.

00:05:23.852 --> 00:05:26.451
What is it that will be your
equivalent of a Snow White?

00:05:26.451 --> 00:05:27.966
Something that's never been done before

00:05:27.966 --> 00:05:29.586
that's really going to get you noticed

00:05:29.586 --> 00:05:32.200
and get the attention
paid to your business.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.327
Lesson number three is stay top of mind.

00:05:35.327 --> 00:05:36.973
Walt Disney did everything he could

00:05:36.973 --> 00:05:40.112
to make sure people kept
remembering the Walt Disney name.

00:05:40.112 --> 00:05:42.452
He did a lot of advertising as an example.

00:05:42.452 --> 00:05:45.123
He did TV campaigns,
direct mail campaigns,

00:05:45.123 --> 00:05:48.383
print ads, he even did
grocery store coupon cutouts.

00:05:48.383 --> 00:05:49.642
So, when you're at the grocery store

00:05:49.642 --> 00:05:52.325
you're thinking about Walt Disney.

00:05:52.325 --> 00:05:55.045
He was also a pioneer in merchandising.

00:05:55.045 --> 00:05:56.926
So, whenever a new feature film came out

00:05:56.926 --> 00:05:58.749
that was a Walt Disney production,

00:05:58.749 --> 00:06:00.602
you would also be able to
buy all the merchandise

00:06:00.602 --> 00:06:02.261
that went along with it.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.771
Today Walt Disney is known
not only for its movies

00:06:04.771 --> 00:06:07.908
but its TV stations, theme parks, dolls,

00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:10.793
toys, games, and a whole
host of other merchandise.

00:06:10.793 --> 00:06:13.874
So, the lesson for entrepreneurs
is stay top of mind.

00:06:13.874 --> 00:06:15.085
You need to do whatever you can

00:06:15.085 --> 00:06:18.248
to make sure your customers
are always thinking about you.

00:06:18.248 --> 00:06:19.980
The easiest way to grow a business

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.662
is to sell more to your
existing customers.

00:06:22.662 --> 00:06:24.272
The hardest way to grow a business

00:06:24.272 --> 00:06:26.722
is to go out and try
to find new customers.

00:06:26.722 --> 00:06:29.041
Do whatever you can to
make sure your customers

00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:30.598
are always thinking about you,

00:06:30.598 --> 00:06:32.038
you're the first person that comes to mind

00:06:32.038 --> 00:06:34.213
when they're thinking about
your product or service

00:06:34.213 --> 00:06:36.549
and it's the best way to be
able to grow your business.

00:06:36.549 --> 00:06:38.592
Walt Disney is an entrepreneurial legend

00:06:38.592 --> 00:06:40.764
who's built up one of the
most recognized companies

00:06:40.764 --> 00:06:41.790
in the world.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.966
But remember, when he first got started

00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:46.852
he had no money, nobody believed in him,

00:06:46.852 --> 00:06:48.355
he had to live out of his office

00:06:48.355 --> 00:06:50.527
because he couldn't afford an apartment.

00:06:50.527 --> 00:06:52.509
He survived on a diet of cold beans

00:06:52.509 --> 00:06:55.223
because he couldn't afford other food.

00:06:55.223 --> 00:06:56.639
By following his lessons, though,

00:06:56.639 --> 00:06:59.565
you, too, can achieve
entrepreneurial success.

00:06:59.565 --> 00:07:02.804
So, remember, find something you love,

00:07:02.804 --> 00:07:06.587
push the boundaries, and stay top of mind.

